=== PROVENANCE ===
Selected groups from the NIST Cryptographic Algorithm Validation Program
(CAVP) GCM test vectors, file gcmEncryptExtIV128.rsp (CAVS 14.0, generated
2012-08-31).

Source      https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/mac/gcmtestvectors.zip
File        gcmEncryptExtIV128.rsp
Retrieved   2026-11-17
SHA-256     30156236f768b0d81e58a3e5bd3bd79ce294cf9ef0ba0a84cf7b869c89ebd9fd
            (of the complete 2.9 MB .rsp file, not of this excerpt)

The complete file is 2.9 MB and holds thousands of cases across every key,
IV, plaintext, AAD and tag length. Checking it in whole would put 2.9 MB of
test data in a teaching repository to exercise a primitive this lab takes
from WebCrypto rather than implements. What it is here to prove is narrower:
that this lab WIRES AES-128-GCM correctly -- key, 96-bit nonce, associated
data, 128-bit tag, in that arrangement -- which is the part a QUIC
implementation gets wrong. So the groups kept are the ones that exercise
that wiring: a 96-bit IV, a 128-bit tag, a plaintext longer than one AES
block, and a non-empty AAD. 3 groups, 45 cases.

Nothing is edited. Each group below is byte-for-byte as the .rsp file prints
it, header lines included.
=== END PROVENANCE ===

